---
import Component from "../../../src/components/donate/GoalMeter.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for the band as /donate ACTUALLY renders it today: no
// Givebutter widget id, real hand-maintained figures, so the component draws
// its own bar.
//
// Unlike `GoalMeter.astro` and `GoalMeter-WithLink.astro` beside it, this page
// needs NO harness override to be visible. Those two demonstrate the widget
// mode, which collapses to nothing in a capture because Givebutter's loader
// never runs — so they force the band open to show their chrome. The static
// mode has no such dependency: `showStatic` is `!widgetId && hasFigures`, so
// with the figures set and the id blank the band renders on its own. What you
// see here is what a visitor sees.
//
// The figures are the real ones as of 2026-09-14: the campaign has not opened,
// so $0 has been raised against a 2026 goal of $10,000 and the bar sits at 0%.
// They replaced $20 of $100,000, which was invented — and which this frame
// exists to make impossible to restore unnoticed. Note that `percent` is what
// the bar is drawn to; it is NOT derived from the two figures, so a non-zero
// value here would draw progress against nothing raised.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: GoalMeter-PreLaunch</title>
    <style is:global>
      /* Page-like width so the heading and the meter sit in their real rhythm;
         the fit-content wrapper would collapse the band to its text. */
      #codeyam-capture {
        width: 1200px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="codeyam-capture">
      <Component
        kicker="Launching soon"
        title="Our 2026 goal: raise $10,000."
        raised="$0"
        goal="$10,000"
        percent={0}
      />
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
